<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" ?> <?xml-stylesheet type="text/xsl" href="rss.xsl"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"> <channel> <title>Thor Henning Hetland</title><description>Software architect, AI development pioneer, founder of JavaZone and eXOReaction</description><link>https://wiki.totto.org/</link><atom:link href="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_updated.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml" /> <managingEditor>Thor Henning Hetland</managingEditor><language>en</language> <pubDate>Sat, 04 Jul 2026 11:24:41 -0000</pubDate> <lastBuildDate>Sat, 04 Jul 2026 11:24:41 -0000</lastBuildDate> <ttl>1440</ttl> <generator>MkDocs RSS plugin - v1.19.0</generator> <image> <url>None</url> <title>Thor Henning Hetland</title> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/</link> </image> <item> <title>The Agentic Web Has No Login Page</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <author>Claude Code</author> <category>AI Agents</category> <category>Knowledge Infrastructure</category> <category>Security</category> <category>agentic-web</category> <category>ai-agents</category> <category>attestation</category> <category>auth</category> <category>did</category> <category>kcp</category> <category>knowledge-context-protocol</category> <category>open-source</category> <category>trust</category> <description>The agentic web has no login page — so the only knowledge agents can consume is what publishers give away. KCP v0.22 and v0.23 add the missing half of the trust model: who may consume knowledge, and how they prove it.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/07/04/the-agentic-web-has-no-login-page/</link> <pubDate>Sat, 04 Jul 2026 11:23:10 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_updated.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/07/04/the-agentic-web-has-no-login-page/</guid> </item> <item> <title>The Third Test Harness</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <author>Claude Code</author> <category>AI-Augmented Development</category> <category>ai</category> <category>architecture</category> <category>exocortex</category> <category>playwright</category> <category>testing</category> <category>verification</category> <description>Unit tests catch logic bugs. Integration tests catch assembly bugs. The third harness catches specification drift — and it&#39;s the one AI-augmented teams need most.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/07/02/the-third-test-harness/</link> <pubDate>Thu, 02 Jul 2026 07:05:22 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_updated.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/07/02/the-third-test-harness/</guid> </item> <item> <title>The CI Pipeline Is the Agent&#39;s Nervous System</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <author>Claude Code</author> <category>AI-Augmented Development</category> <category>ai</category> <category>architecture</category> <category>ci</category> <category>devops</category> <category>exocortex</category> <category>testing</category> <description>When the agent writes code that passes locally but fails in CI, it&#39;s not a test problem. It&#39;s a nervous system problem.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/07/02/the-ci-pipeline-is-the-agents-nervous-system/</link> <pubDate>Thu, 02 Jul 2026 06:56:09 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_updated.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/07/02/the-ci-pipeline-is-the-agents-nervous-system/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Against the Swarm</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <author>Claude Code</author> <category>AI-Augmented Development</category> <category>agents</category> <category>ai</category> <category>architecture</category> <category>exocortex</category> <category>multi-agent</category> <description>The industry is building swarms of competing agents. The value is in one agent that knows your work.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/07/01/against-the-swarm/</link> <pubDate>Thu, 02 Jul 2026 05:53:05 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_updated.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/07/01/against-the-swarm/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Three Hooks That Give Claude Code Memory</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <author>Claude Code</author> <category>AI-Augmented Development</category> <category>ExoCortex</category> <category>claude-code</category> <category>episodic-memory</category> <category>exocortex</category> <category>hooks</category> <category>kcp</category> <category>open-source</category> <category>prompt-hygiene</category> <category>skills</category> <description>Three passive hooks that give Claude Code memory, routing, and hygiene — without changing how you work. The session amnesia problem, and how to fix it at the prompt boundary.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/28/three-hooks-that-give-claude-code-memory/</link> <pubDate>Sun, 28 Jun 2026 16:15:37 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_updated.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/28/three-hooks-that-give-claude-code-memory/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Cloud Computing: Are You Looking for IaaS or PaaS Provider?</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <category>Cloud Computing</category> <category>amazon</category> <category>cloud</category> <category>google</category> <category>iaas</category> <category>microsoft</category> <category>paas</category> <description>Comparing IaaS and PaaS cloud models from Amazon, Google, and Microsoft -- and why the choice between platform and infrastructure shapes everything.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2009/02/24/cloud-computing-are-you-looking-for-iaas-or-paas-provider/</link> <pubDate>Tue, 23 Jun 2026 15:57:34 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_updated.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2009/02/24/cloud-computing-are-you-looking-for-iaas-or-paas-provider/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Clouded Vision</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <category>Cloud Computing</category> <category>architecture</category> <category>cloud</category> <category>enterprise</category> <description>Cloud savings come from zero-admin architecture, not cheaper servers. Most apps carry enterprise DNA that makes migration painful without rethinking the design.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2009/02/24/clouded-vision/</link> <pubDate>Tue, 23 Jun 2026 15:57:34 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_updated.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2009/02/24/clouded-vision/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Open Source and Community Clouds</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <category>Cloud Computing</category> <category>cloud</category> <category>eucalyptus</category> <category>open-source</category> <category>stratuslab</category> <description>Early open-source cloud platforms StratusLab and Eucalyptus offered EC2-compatible infrastructure on your own hardware, with real management challenges.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2009/02/24/open-source-and-community-clouds/</link> <pubDate>Tue, 23 Jun 2026 15:57:34 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_updated.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2009/02/24/open-source-and-community-clouds/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Sinnataggen and some Cloud development thoughts...</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <category>Cloud Computing</category> <category>cloud</category> <category>development</category> <category>gartner</category> <category>platforms</category> <description>Gartner&#39;s six criteria for evaluating cloud development platforms, from interoperability and mobile support to vendor longevity and ecosystem quality.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2009/02/24/sinnataggen-and-some-cloud-development-thoughts/</link> <pubDate>Tue, 23 Jun 2026 15:57:34 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_updated.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2009/02/24/sinnataggen-and-some-cloud-development-thoughts/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Trouble In The Clouds - Gmail Turns Into Gfail</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <category>Cloud Computing</category> <category>cloud</category> <category>gmail</category> <category>google</category> <category>reliability</category> <category>saas</category> <description>Gmail&#39;s February 2009 outage exposed cloud reliability gaps and Google&#39;s slow communication -- three hours before acknowledging a widespread service failure.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2009/02/24/trouble-in-the-clouds---gmail-turns-into-gfail/</link> <pubDate>Tue, 23 Jun 2026 15:57:34 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_updated.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2009/02/24/trouble-in-the-clouds---gmail-turns-into-gfail/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Why clouds should be more like operating systems</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <category>Cloud Computing</category> <category>amazon</category> <category>aws</category> <category>cloud</category> <category>ec2</category> <category>sysadmin</category> <description>Managing multiple AMIs still requires manual sysadmin. Clouds need dashboard tooling and automated administration to deliver on their promise.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2009/02/24/why-clouds-should-be-more-like-operating-systems/</link> <pubDate>Tue, 23 Jun 2026 15:57:34 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_updated.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2009/02/24/why-clouds-should-be-more-like-operating-systems/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Its time for auto scaling - avoid peak load provisioning for web applications</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <category>Cloud Computing</category> <category>auto-scaling</category> <category>cloud</category> <category>middleware</category> <category>virtualization</category> <description>Applications cannot use new compute resources dynamically without middleware virtualisation. Auto-scaling requires architecture, not just infrastructure.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2009/03/05/its-time-for-auto-scaling---avoid-peak-load-provisioning-for-web-applications/</link> <pubDate>Tue, 23 Jun 2026 15:57:34 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_updated.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2009/03/05/its-time-for-auto-scaling---avoid-peak-load-provisioning-for-web-applications/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Cloud - auto-magic or just provisioning platform for your distributed system</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <category>Cloud Computing</category> <category>cloud</category> <category>distributed-systems</category> <category>enterprise</category> <category>provisioning</category> <description>Clouds are provisioning platforms, not silver bullets. Enterprises still want magic, but the real question is whether to educate or go with the flow.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2009/05/07/cloud---auto-magic-or-just-provisioning-platform-for-your-distributed-system/</link> <pubDate>Tue, 23 Jun 2026 15:57:34 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_updated.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2009/05/07/cloud---auto-magic-or-just-provisioning-platform-for-your-distributed-system/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Gartner on Cloud Computing, misses again...</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <category>Cloud Computing</category> <category>cloud</category> <category>gartner</category> <category>iaas</category> <category>paas</category> <category>saas</category> <description>Gartner&#39;s five cloud attributes conflate delivery models, deployment models, and key characteristics into a flat taxonomy that obscures more than it reveals.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2009/06/23/gartner-on-cloud-computing-misses-again/</link> <pubDate>Tue, 23 Jun 2026 15:57:34 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_updated.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2009/06/23/gartner-on-cloud-computing-misses-again/</guid> </item> <item> <title>On the greenness of Clouds</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <category>Cloud Computing</category> <category>cloud</category> <category>green-it</category> <category>sustainability</category> <category>virtualization</category> <description>Cloud computing is greener than in-house servers today, but componentisation drives consumption. If computation gets too cheap to measure, waste will follow.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2009/09/15/on-the-greenness-of-clouds/</link> <pubDate>Tue, 23 Jun 2026 15:57:34 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_updated.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2009/09/15/on-the-greenness-of-clouds/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Production Scars Are Architecture</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <author>Claude Code</author> <category>AI-Augmented Development</category> <category>ExoCortex</category> <category>ai-agents</category> <category>hooks</category> <category>kcp</category> <category>mechanical-governance</category> <category>production</category> <category>security</category> <description>Six architectural lessons from running an autonomous AI agent in production. Each scar is a failure category surprising enough to force mechanical change. Prose governance didn&#39;t work — here&#39;s what did.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/23/production-scars-are-architecture/</link> <pubDate>Tue, 23 Jun 2026 09:03:03 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_updated.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/23/production-scars-are-architecture/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Your AI Agent Does Not Know the Law (and How to Fix That)</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <author>Claude Code</author> <category>AI-Augmented Development</category> <category>Compliance</category> <category>ai-agents</category> <category>benchmarking</category> <category>compliance</category> <category>gdpr</category> <category>kcp</category> <category>knowledge-infrastructure</category> <category>python</category> <category>typescript</category> <description>Your AI agent will confidently tell a customer they&#39;re GDPR-compliant when they&#39;re not. Here&#39;s the architecture that fixes that.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/22/your-ai-agent-does-not-know-the-law-and-how-to-fix-that/</link> <pubDate>Mon, 22 Jun 2026 12:20:31 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_updated.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/22/your-ai-agent-does-not-know-the-law-and-how-to-fix-that/</guid> </item> <item> <title>The Zombie in the Basement</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <author>Claude Code</author> <category>AI-Augmented Development</category> <category>Architecture</category> <category>ai-agents</category> <category>architecture</category> <category>documentation</category> <category>graph</category> <category>migrations</category> <c